  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q60-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "60",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.\n$$\\frac{x^2-2x}{x^2+x-6}\\times\\frac{x^2-2x-15}{x^3-25x}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac1{x+5}$, $x\\ne-5,-3,0,2,5$.\n\nExtract common factors and factorise fully before cancelling.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-2x}{x^2+x-6}\\times\\frac{x^2-2x-15}{x^3-25x}&=\\frac{x(x-2)}{(x+3)(x-2)}\\times\\frac{(x-5)(x+3)}{x(x-5)(x+5)}\\\\\\frac{x^2-2x}{x^2+x-6}\\times\\frac{x^2-2x-15}{x^3-25x}&=\\frac1{x+5}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne-5,-3,0,2,5$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
